---
id: doctrine-missions-recon-map
title: Recon Map — Doctrine Missions
summary: One-pass recon for the Doctrine Missions feature — collapses a doctrine's paired .yaml + .design.md + separate Knight files into a directory of prose (design.md + missions/*.md) and removes the Knight entity outright. Covers relevant codex, the binding ADR/standards table, the verified code surface (including two undocumented touch points — frontmatter_edit.py's "doctrine" kind and src/lore/defaults/gitignore), lane scope, and four named conflicts/gaps the PRD leaves open.
---

# Recon Map — Doctrine Missions

**Author:** Recon
**Date:** 2026-09-15
**Feature:** Doctrine becomes a directory of prose (`<doctrine>.design.md` + `missions/<id>.md`); the Knight entity is removed outright.
**Upstream PRD:** `doctrine-missions-prd`

---

## 1. Relevant Codex

| ID | Title | Why relevant |
|----|-------|-------------|
| `doctrine-missions-prd` | Doctrine Missions — PRD | Upstream, authoritative on scope and settled product decisions. |
| `conceptual-entities-doctrine` | Doctrine | Current two-file model (design.md + yaml); every claim here about steps/YAML schema is being replaced. |
| `conceptual-entities-knight` | Knight | The entity being removed outright; documents what/how separation now folding into mission files. |
| `conceptual-entities-mission` | Mission | Lore's own DB entity — the name collision partner for "doctrine mission." Documents the `knight` field being renamed. |
| `conceptual-relationships-doctrine--knight` | Doctrine to Knight | The relationship being deleted; documents today's unenforced-reference model this feature's `doctrine_mission` reference inherits the *shape* of. |
| `conceptual-relationships-doctrine--mission` | Doctrine to Mission | Documents step→Mission field mapping (`step.knight` → `mission.knight`) that becomes `doctrine_mission` → `missions.doctrine_mission`. |
| `conceptual-relationships-knight--mission` | Knight to Mission | The `missions.knight` column and its resolve-at-show-time model — the direct precedent for `missions.doctrine_mission`. |
| `conceptual-relationships-artifact--doctrine` | Artifact to Doctrine | Step notes reference artifacts by free-text ID; same pattern likely carries into mission-file bodies. |
| `conceptual-relationships-watcher--doctrine` | Watcher to Doctrine | Watcher `action:` names a doctrine by stem — unaffected by this feature (doctrine id resolution is unchanged), included for completeness. |
