## 4. Lane Coverage

| Lane | In scope? | Why |
|------|-----------|-----|
| foundation — leaf modules with zero or near-zero `lore.*` imports | yes | `paths.py` (drop `knights_dir`), `schemas/` + 3 packaged YAML files (one deleted, one added, `__init__.py`'s dispatch table edited). `validators.py`, `ids.py`, `frontmatter.py`, `initplan.py`, `graph.py`, `config.py`, `root.py` are **not** touched — no validator or path-construction rule this feature needs is missing from what exists today; `frontmatter.py`'s existing `parse_frontmatter_doc` is reused as-is for mission files. `safewrite.py` is in scope only if the atomicity gap noted in §3/§5 is closed here rather than deferred. |
| core — storage, entity modules, business logic | yes | `db.py`, `models.py`, `migrations/`, `doctrine.py` (rewritten), `knight.py` (deleted), `health.py`, `init.py` (seed new shape / drop knight seeding), `skills.py` (retire `update-knight`), `reconcile.py` (remove seeded knights, reseed doctrines). `watcher.py`, `artifact.py`, `codex.py`, `glossary.py`, `impacts.py`, `priority.py`, `oracle.py`, `agents.py`, rites — **not** touched: none of these read or write the `knight`/`doctrine` shape directly (watcher's `action:` and artifact's step-note references are opaque strings unaffected by the entity's internal shape change). |
| surface — `api.py`, `cli.py`, `prompts.py` | yes, except `prompts.py` | `api.py` (remove 6 knight names + `_knight` alias, update doctrine signatures), `cli.py` (remove `knight` command group, rewrite `doctrine new/edit/show`, drop `"knights"` from health `--scope` Choice). `prompts.py` is **not** touched — no `lore init` prompt names knights or doctrines by entity type; it prompts on agents/access-mode/skill-families/gitignore policy only. |

`src/lore/defaults/` (scribe territory, not a dev lane) is large here: 4 doctrines, 12 knights, 5 lore-design-documents artifacts, 10 skills, 2 docs on disk today — of which this feature's own FR list scopes exactly 4 doctrines converted, 12 knight files folded away, 2 artifacts touched, 5 skills touched (1 retired + 4 updated), and both docs updated. Say so explicitly per the mission brief: this is real, sizeable content-authoring work, distinct from the code lanes above.

